  "name": "HEAVY METAL WATER",
  "code": "1112",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"117\" data-end=\"425\">The <strong data-start=\"121\" data-end=\"147\">Heavy Metal Water Test</strong> is performed to detect the presence and concentration of toxic metals (such as <strong data-start=\"227\" data-end=\"284\">lead, arsenic, cadmium, mercury, chromium, and others</strong>) in water samples. It is essential for assessing <strong data-start=\"334\" data-end=\"359\">drinking water safety</strong>, especially in residential, industrial, or agricultural settings.</p>\n<p data-start=\"427\" data-end=\"474\"><strong data-start=\"430\" data-end=\"474\">Clinical and Environmental Significance:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"475\" data-end=\"759\">\n<li data-start=\"475\" data-end=\"563\">\n<p data-start=\"477\" data-end=\"563\">Helps identify <strong data-start=\"492\" data-end=\"522\">contaminated water sources</strong> that may lead to long-term health risks.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"564\" data-end=\"669\">\n<p data-start=\"566\" data-end=\"669\">Crucial for <strong data-start=\"578\" data-end=\"606\">preventive public health</strong> and <strong data-start=\"611\" data-end=\"636\">regulatory compliance</strong> (e.g., WHO, EPA, BIS standards).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"670\" data-end=\"759\">\n<p data-start=\"672\" data-end=\"759\">Important for populations exposed to <strong data-start=\"709\" data-end=\"734\">industrial pollutants</strong> or using <strong data-start=\"744\" data-end=\"758\">well water</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Elevated Heavy Metals in Water</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Possible Health/Environmental Impact</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Lead</strong></td>\n<td>Neurological damage, especially in children; developmental delays</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Arsenic</strong></td>\n<td>Skin changes, increased cancer risk, cardiovascular and neurological effects</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Cadmium</strong></td>\n<td>Kidney damage, bone loss, increased cancer risk</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Mercury</strong></td>\n<td>Neurological and developmental disorders, kidney toxicity</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Chromium (especially Cr VI)</strong></td>\n<td>Skin irritation, carcinogenic effects</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
